
* How to use Git and create GitHub account?

1. Create 2 Ec2 instances:- (a) Mumbai.git (b) Singapore.git = Security group - SSH, HTTP {Allow both}
2. Then Login in mumbai instance using Putty or MobaXterm

Commands-


- Sudo su
- yum update -y
- yum install git -y          (which git)
- git --version
- git config --global user.name "user-name"
- git config --global user.email "user-emali-id"
- git config --list           (It will display user-name & mail-id)


# Same process for Singapore- Then create Github account & Login

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


* How to add, commit in Local Repo, How to push code and pull code from GitHub?


[MUMBAI EC2 INSTANCE]

1. Login into mumbai instance
2. Create a Directory and go inside it

Commands-


- git init                    (Directory convert into local repo)
- touch <file-name>           (put some data in this file)
- git add .                   (. means if anything in the file then add the all)
- git commit -m "my 1st commit from mumbai.git"
- git status
- git log                     (it tells you who's commit/ which user commit this)
- git show <commit-id>        (it will dispaly all codes that you have written)
- git remote add origin <Central Git URL>
- git push -u origin master
  (Enter Username & Password)


#NOTE:-  If the password not working do this process --

* Authentication: GitHub no longer accepts account passwords on the command line. When asked, use a Personal Access Token
* Personal Access Token (PAT)

Use this if you don’t want to install anything extra. The token acts as your password.

1. Log in to github.com, click your profile picture (top right) → Settings.
2. Scroll down the left sidebar and click Developer settings.
3. Click Personal access tokens → Tokens (classic).
4. Click Generate new token → Generate new token (classic).
5. Fill in:

> Note: something like my-laptop
> Expiration: choose a duration (30 or 90 days is fine)
> Scopes: tick repo

6. Click Generate token at the bottom.
7. Copy the token immediately. GitHub shows it only once. Save it somewhere safe, like a password manager.
8. Run git push. When asked:

Username: your GitHub username
Password: paste the token (not your account password). The terminal won’t show characters as you paste, which is normal.



#*#->  NOW GO TO SINGAPORE EC2 INSTANCE CREATE ONE DIRECTORY AND GO INSIDE IT----


Commands-

- git init
- git remote add origin <GitHub Repo URL>
- git pull -u origin master
- git log
- git pull origin master                (Now you can see- it pull all the code )
- git show <commit-id>

# Now add some data/code in the file

- git status
- git add .
- git commit -m "Singapore Update1"
- git status
- git log
- git push origin master

# Now go to mumbai ec2 instance

- git log
- git pull origin master
- git log
- git show <commit-id>-


